Dear Hiring Team,

I am pleased to apply for the *Software Engineer I* position with *The Walt Disney Company*. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience, a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, and hands-on experience developing full-stack applications across UI, API, and data layers. Disney's need for robust data integration capabilities within Rights Management particularly resonates with my work building production systems that connect users, services, and governed business data.

At Sperse, I designed, developed, tested, and deployed a full-stack workflow application using React and TypeScript, RESTful APIs, and PostgreSQL for more than 10,000 users. I also built a Python/FastAPI integration layer exposing 160+ validated backend actions to Generative AI APIs and intelligent automation features, then integrated machine learning models through LangGraph and LangChain across 40+ specialized agents. To support reliable operations, I investigated production incidents with Redis telemetry and OpenTelemetry traces and added CI/CD quality gates for latency, accuracy, and safety. This combination prepares me to contribute across Disney's UI, API, and data layers while integrating AI capabilities responsibly.

Previously at Qualitest, I designed a Java/Spring Boot RESTful service backed by PostgreSQL and Redis for file operations across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I improved SQL performance with window functions, materialized views, and indexes, delivered React/JavaScript visualizations for business stakeholders, and strengthened error recovery across 100K+ weekly AWS Step Functions executions. Across both roles, I collaborated with cross-functional teams to refine user stories, conduct peer reviews, resolve application issues, and deploy maintainable software with Git, Jenkins, and Docker—experience aligned with the agile, collaborative environment described for Rights & Accounting.

Disney's mission to entertain, inform, and inspire people around the globe through unparalleled storytelling is compelling because it places technology in service of meaningful audience experiences. I would welcome the opportunity to bring curiosity, quality-focused engineering, and a commitment to creativity and innovation to the Content Platforms & Operations organization as it advances the systems that govern and track content rights and availability. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

